lesson: 151
title: A fraction of a quantity
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: To find a fraction of a quantity, first find one equal part: divide by the number below the line.
explain: Then take as many parts as the number above the line says: multiply.
explain: Three fifths of a 40 km road: one fifth is 40 ÷ 5 = 8 km, so three fifths is 3 × 8 = 24 km.
vars: a=name u=3..40 p=3..10 m=2..9
let: n = p * u
need: m < p
need: (m % 2 != 0 || p % 2 != 0) && (m % 3 != 0 || p % 3 != 0) && (m % 5 != 0 || p % 5 != 0)
answer: u * m
exercise: A ribbon is {n} cm long. {a} cuts off {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of it. How many centimetres does {a.he} cut off?
exercise: {a} has {n} dollars and spends {m}/{p} of the money on a bike. How many dollars does the bike cost?
exercise: The road from the village to the town is {n} km long. A bus has driven {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of the way. How many kilometres has the bus driven?
exercise: A tank holds {n} litres of water when it is full. Now it is {m}/{p} full. How many litres of water are in it?
exercise: Find {m}/{p} of {n} kg.
exercise: A farmer has {n} sheep, and {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of them are white. How many white sheep does the farmer have?
test: The painters have finished {m}/{p} of a fence {n} metres long. How many metres have they painted?
test: How many grams is {m}/{p} of a {n}-gram bag of flour?
test: {a}'s book has {n} pages, and {a.he} has read {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of it. How many pages has {a.he} read?
test: On a trip of {n} km, the family drove {m}/{p} of the distance before lunch and the rest after it. How many kilometres did they drive before lunch?
exercise: What is {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of {n}?
exercise: A class in Ohio has {n} dollars for a trip and spends {m}/{p} of it on the bus. How many dollars does the bus cost?
exercise: {a} picked {n} strawberries on a farm in Kent and ate {m}/{p} of them. How many strawberries did {a.he} eat?
exercise: Of the {n} pupils at a school in Ontario, {m}/{p} walk to school. How many pupils walk?
exercise: A cake recipe from Sydney uses {n} grams of sugar. {a} makes {m}/{p} of the recipe. How many grams of sugar does {a.he} use?
exercise: A farmer in Ireland has a field of {n} square metres and plants potatoes on {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of it. How many square metres are planted with potatoes?
exercise: {m}/{p} of the {n} seats in a cinema in Auckland are taken. How many seats are taken?
exercise: A hike is {n} km long, and {a} has walked {m}/{p} of it so far. How many kilometres has {a.he} walked?
test: How many minutes is {m}/{p} of {n} minutes?
test: There are {n} books in a classroom in Wales, and {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of them are storybooks. How many storybooks are there?
test: {a} saved {n} dollars and gave {m}/{p} of the savings to a charity in Toronto. How many dollars did {a.he} give?
test: A water barrel holds {n} litres when it is full. It is {m.words} {p.ordwords}s full now. How many litres are in the barrel?
test: Workers have repaired {m}/{p} of the road near Dublin, which is {n} km long. How many kilometres of the road are repaired?
test: Out of {n} apples picked in an orchard in Washington State, {m}/{p} are red. How many red apples are there?
exercise: ribbon's {n} cm, {a} cuts off {m}/{p} of it. how many cm is that
exercise: got {n} dollars, spent {m}/{p} on a bike. bike cost?
exercise: {n+10} metres of fence — no wait, {n} m — painted {m}/{p} so far. how many metres done
exercise: my mate says {m}/{p} of {n} is {n} ÷ {p} = {u}. nah he forgot the top bit. what's {m}/{p} of {n}
test: {n} km trip, done {m}/{p} of it already, and we stopped twice for snacks. how many km done
test: {m}/{p} of {a}'s {n} stickers are shiny. how many shiny ones
test: {a} reckons {m}/{p} of {n} is {n} × {m}, way too big innit. what is it for real
exam: It is given that a ribbon measures {n} cm in length, of which {m}/{p} is cut off. Determine the length of the portion so cut off, in centimetres.
exam: Whereas {a} possessed {n} dollars and expended {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of that sum upon a bicycle, ascertain the cost of the bicycle in dollars.
exam: Ascertain the mass, in kilograms, of {m}/{p} of a consignment of flour whose total mass is {n} kilograms.
exam: A consignment of {n} books is received by a library, and {m}/{p} of the consignment is assigned to the children's section. State the number of books so assigned.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {n} dollars, and {a} got {m.words} {p.ordwords}s of it. How many dollars did {a} get?
exercise: Since {a}'s dad was let go, the family's {n} dollars a month has to stretch further, and {m}/{p} of it goes on rent. How many dollars is the rent?
test: {a} says {a.he} "only had a bit" of the {n}-gram cake — creative with the truth, it was {m}/{p} of it. how many grams did the greedy sod eat
